## Executive Summary

GPT-6.1 Sol is OpenAI's mid-priced GPT-6 model, released September 29, 2026, designed for complex coding, computer use, and professional work with near-Astra intelligence at one-fifth of the cost. It features a massive 1.05M token context window, competitive pricing ($2/$10 per 1M tokens), and exceptional performance across agentic coding and computer use benchmarks. The model ranks #7 of 27 models on the Vals Index with 63.94% and achieves 52 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index (comparable to GPT-6 Astra). GPT-6.1 Sol delivers substantial gains over its predecessor GPT-6 Sol, more than doubling Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1 score at maximum reasoning effort while costing less than half per task. The model is positioned as OpenAI's most cost-effective flagship model, offering near-Astra intelligence for complex coding, research, and computer use at 80% lower cost than GPT-6 Astra ($2/$10 vs $10/$50). It also ranks #2 of 43 on Terminal-Bench-Science, demonstrating strong scientific workflow capabilities.

