## Model Identity and Background

**Developer:** OpenAI
**Release Date:** September 29, 2026
**Series:** GPT-6.1 (GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6.1 Terra, GPT-6.1 Luna)
**Predecessor:** GPT-6 Sol (September 22, 2026) — replaced after just 7 days
**Successor:** No successor yet
**License:** Proprietary
**Context Window:** 1,050,000 tokens
**Max Output:** 128,000 tokens

GPT-6.1 Sol is OpenAI's mid-priced GPT-6 model, released September 29, 2026, replacing GPT-6 Sol after just 7 days. The model is designed for complex coding, computer use, and professional work, with near-Astra intelligence at one-fifth of the cost. GPT-6.1 Sol represents a significant improvement over its predecessor, delivering more than double the score on Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1 at maximum reasoning effort while costing less than half per task. The model is positioned as OpenAI's most cost-effective flagship model, offering competitive performance to GPT-6 Astra while remaining significantly cheaper.

