GPT-6.1 Sol achieves more than double the score of GPT-6 Sol on Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1 at maximum reasoning effort, demonstrating strong scientific workflow capabilities.

### Artificial Analysis Benchmarks
**Source:** Artificial Analysis
**Snapshot:** October 2026

- Intelligence Index: 52 (verified, comparable to GPT-6 Astra's 53)
- Speed: 58.8 tokens per second (verified)
- Time to first token: 162.10s (verified, faster than GPT-6 Astra's 267.84s)
- Cost per Intelligence Index task: Not available

GPT-6.1 Sol achieves 52 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index, comparable to GPT-6 Astra's 53. The model is faster than GPT-6 Astra (58.8 vs 67.8 tokens/second) and has a lower time to first token (162.10s vs 267.84s).

### ExploitBench Benchmark
**Source:** OpenAI internal benchmarks
**Snapshot:** September 2026

- ExploitBench - Internal Port: 21.5% (verified, arbitrary code-execution success rate)
- GPT-6 Astra: 31.5% (verified)
- GPT-6 Sol: 5.5% (verified)
- GPT-5.6 Sol: 3.5% (verified)

GPT-6.1 Sol reaches an arbitrary code-execution success rate of 21.5% on ExploitBench, substantially stronger than the earlier Sol models (5.5% for GPT-6 Sol, 3.5% for GPT-5.6 Sol), while remaining below GPT-6 Astra (31.5%).

